IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpfta-types`

-- Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, Part 4 (ss 35 to 44) and the
-- Third Schedule (repealed).  Source: source/CPFTA2003.txt lines 2196 to 2386.

§ `Part 4 -- General`

§§ `35. No contracting out`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 35(1) and (3)"
GIVEN c IS A `Contracting Out Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract term is void to the extent that it is inconsistent with the Act` IF
        c's `the term is contained in a contract, or is an agreement to the contrary`
    AND c's `the term is inconsistent with the provisions of the Act`
    AND NOT c's `the release was made by a person in settlement of a dispute`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 35(2) and (3)"
GIVEN c IS A `Contracting Out Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the waiver or release is void` IF
        c's `the term is a waiver or release of a right, benefit or protection conferred under the Act`
    AND NOT c's `the release was made by a person in settlement of a dispute`

§§ `36. Rights transferred`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 36"
GIVEN s IS A `Successor Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual has the same rights as the consumer to seek and obtain redress from the supplier` IF
        s's `the individual is an heir or assignee of a consumer`
    AND s's `the individual receives goods or services`
    AND NOT s's `the individual receives them in the course of business`

§§ `37. Preservation of other rights or remedies`

-- 37(1): nothing in the Act restricts, limits or derogates from any other right or
-- remedy of a consumer, subject to 37(2): any provision to the contrary in regulations
-- made under s 11 or s 43.  No such regulations are an input, so whether they exist is
-- a fact the caller supplies.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 37(1) and (2)"
GIVEN `regulations made under section 11 or 43 provide to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act restricts, limits or derogates from a right or remedy the consumer has apart from the Act` IF
    `regulations made under section 11 or 43 provide to the contrary`

§§ `38. Exemption from liability for publishers`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 38"
GIVEN p IS A `Publisher Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is not liable under the Act in respect of the advertisement` IF
        p's `the person prints, publishes, distributes, broadcasts or telecasts an advertisement on behalf of a supplier`
    AND p's `the person does so in good faith`
    AND p's `the person does so in the ordinary course of the person's business`

§§ `39. Parol evidence rule abolished`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 39(1) and (2)"
GIVEN p IS A `Parol Evidence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 39 makes the parol or extrinsic evidence admissible` IF
        p's `the evidence is parol or extrinsic evidence establishing the existence of an express warranty`
    AND p's `the action relates to a consumer transaction between a consumer and a supplier`
    AND NOT p's `the goods or services are intended for business use`

§§ `40. Interpretation of documents`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 40(a) and (b)"
GIVEN d IS A `Document Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision must be interpreted against the supplier` IF
        d's `a consumer and a supplier enter into a consumer transaction`
    AND d's `all or part of the transaction or contract is evidenced by a document provided by the supplier`
    AND d's `a provision of the document is ambiguous`

§§ `41. Burden of proof`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 41(1) and (2)"
GIVEN b IS A `Burden Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the burden of proving compliance is on the supplier` IF
        b's `the proceedings are taken in a court between a consumer and a supplier in relation to a consumer transaction`
    AND b's `a dispute arises as to whether the supplier has complied with a requirement`
    AND b's `the requirement is specified by regulations made under section 41(2)`

-- 41(3): the section does not affect any other rule of law placing a burden of proof
-- on the supplier: a saving, inert.

§§ `42 and 43. Amendment of Schedules; Regulations`

-- Section 42 lets the Minister amend the Schedules by order in the Gazette, and s 43
-- lets the Minister make regulations, with fourteen listed purposes in s 43(2)(a) to
-- (n).  Both are powers with no fallback of their own, and no order or regulation is
-- an input.  The Schedules are encoded as printed (First Schedule as amended by
-- G.N. No. S 387/2016, as the printed text records).

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 42"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no orders under section 42 amending the Schedules after the date of the printed text are encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "no orders under section 42 amending the Schedules after the date of the printed text are encoded in this model"

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 43(1) and (2)(a) to (n)"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no regulations under section 43 are encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "no regulations under section 43 are encoded in this model"

§§ `44. Saving and transitional provisions`

-- 44(1), (2), (3): matters commenced by, or orders made in relation to, the Standards,
-- Productivity and Innovation Board before 2 April 2018 and pending or unsatisfied on
-- that date pass to the Commission.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 44(1) and (3)"
GIVEN t IS A `Transitional Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commission may continue the matter as if it had commenced it` IF
        t's `the matter was commenced or made by, or in relation to, the Standards, Productivity and Innovation Board`
    AND t's `the date on which it was commenced or made` LESS THAN YMD 2018 4 2
    AND t's `it is pending, or the order remains unsatisfied, on 2 April 2018`
    AND (CONSIDER t's `kind of matter`
         WHEN `proceedings for a declaration or an injunction under section 9 or 10` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an investigation under Part 3A` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an order of the District Court or the High Court under section 9 or 10 requiring a person to notify, inform, reimburse or do anything in relation to the Board` THEN FALSE)

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 44(2)"
GIVEN t IS A `Transitional Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unsatisfied order is satisfied` IF
        t's `the matter was commenced or made by, or in relation to, the Standards, Productivity and Innovation Board`
    AND t's `the date on which it was commenced or made` LESS THAN YMD 2018 4 2
    AND t's `it is pending, or the order remains unsatisfied, on 2 April 2018`
    AND t's `the person notifies, informs, reimburses or does the thing in relation to the Commission`
    AND (CONSIDER t's `kind of matter`
         WHEN `an order of the District Court or the High Court under section 9 or 10 requiring a person to notify, inform, reimburse or do anything in relation to the Board` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

-- 44(4) defines "Board".  The Third Schedule is repealed by Act 25 of 2016 and has
-- no content.
